## Python Instruction
Write a python function to find the number of ways to partition a set of n elements into k non-empty subsets.

## Python Solution
```python
def partition_Ways(n, k):
    # Bell number
    bell = [[0 for _ in range(n+1)] for _ in range(n+1)]
    bell[0][0] = 1
    for i in range(1, n+1):
        bell[i][0] = bell[i-1][i-1]
        for j in range(1, i+1):
            bell[i][j] = bell[i-1][j-1] + bell[i-1][j]
    # Stirling number of the second kind
    stirling = [[0 for _ in range(n+1)] for _ in range(n+1)]
    for i in range(n+1):
        stirling[i][0] = 0
        stirling[i][i] = 1
        for j in range(1, i+1):
            stirling[i][j] = j * stirling[i-1][j] + stirling[i-1][j-1]
    # Partition ways
    return stirling[n][k]
```

## Python Tests
